1. sastrawijs
   License: MIT
   Homepage: https://github.com/damzaky/sastrawijs
   Used for: Indonesian word stemming (Nazief-Adriani algorithm) in the
   default `id` pipeline.

   Provenance note (research R4): the Sastrawi root-word dictionary is
   derived from the kateglo.com word list, which is published under
   CC BY-NC-SA 3.0 (non-commercial). sastrawijs itself is distributed under
   the MIT license. If non-commercial terms are incompatible with a given
   redistribution, the `stem()` contract is engine-agnostic and the root-word
   list can be swapped behind the unchanged API (documented in README,
   "Upstream capabilities").

2. hyphen
   License: ISC
   Homepage: https://github.com/ytiurin/hyphen
   Used for: hyphenation pattern lookups (`id`, `en`) driving the soft-hyphen
   line-breaking feature. Indonesian and English patterns are sourced from
   the hyphenation pattern archive distributed with this package.

3. minisearch
   License: MIT
   Homepage: https://github.com/lucaong/minisearch
   Used for: client-side full-text search engine backing the offline search
   index and the setup-free `ui: 'nav'` / `ui: 'external'` search dialog.

4. stemmer
   License: MIT
   Homepage: https://github.com/words/stemmer
   Used for: English (Porter) stemming when `language: 'en'`.

5. stopwords-iso
   License: MIT
   Homepage: https://github.com/stopwords-iso/stopwords-iso
   Used for: the vendored Indonesian (`id`) and English (`en`) stop-word
   lists, generated into src/core/stopwords/ by scripts/update-stopwords.ts
   and shipped in the package. The generated files state their source key and
   entry count on the first line.